States and internationally. It operates through three segments: Healthcare, Education, and Commercial. The company offers financial and operational performance improvement consulting services; digital services; spanning technology and analytic-related services, including enterprise health record, enterprise resource planning, enterprise performance management, customer relationship management, data management, artificial intelligence and automation, technology managed services, and a portfolio of software products; organizational transformation; revenue cycle managed services and outsourcing; financial and capital advisory consulting; and strategy and innovation consulting. It also provides research-focused consulting and managed services, as well as Huron Research product suite, a software suite designed to facilitate and improve research administration service delivery and compliance. In addition, the company offers software products, financial capital advisory services, regulatory compliance and risk management consulting, and Commercial consulting. The company serves healthcare, education, financial services, industrials and manufacturing, energy and utilities, public sector, and other commercial industries. The company was incorporated in 2002 and is headquartered in Chicago, Illinois.","ceo_bio":"Mr. C. Mark Hussey C.F.A., C.M.A., CPA, M.B.A. | President, CEO & Director | Age 64 | Compensation: $2.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 9K people. Revenue per employee of $178K ranks in the bottom quartile among Industrials peers, improving at 7%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $19K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $5K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 15\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Huron Consulting Group Inc. is a mid-cap industrials business with a $2.6B market cap on $1.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +14% over the past three years and +8% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 11% against a 8% cost of capital, a 3-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $183M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 11 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.84\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 5.2\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 6.3% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 2.7% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Goodwill represents 52% of total assets \u2014 a large impairment risk hanging over book value","sev":"red","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.7% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $4.8M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Industrials peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 8% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Industrials ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"news_headlines":[{"title":"3 Reasons Why Growth Investors Shouldn't Overlook Huron Consulting (HURN)","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3024705/3-reasons-why-growth-investors-shouldn-t-overlook-huron-consulting-hurn?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_11_growth-3024705","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793897102.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.382,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Wall Street Analysts See a 25.42% Upside in Huron Consulting (HURN): Can the Stock Really Move This High?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3024390/wall-street-analysts-see-a-25-42-upside-in-huron-consulting-hurn-can-the-stock-really-move-this-high?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cconsensus_price_target-3024390","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793886902.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Are Business Services Stocks Lagging  Huron Consulting Group (HURN) This Year?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3024301/are-business-services-stocks-lagging-huron-consulting-group-hurn-this-year?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_1-3024301","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793886002.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.273,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Huron Consulting Group (HURN) Stock Looks Reasonable Following Its 225% Five Year Run","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/commercial-services/nasdaq-hurn/huron-consulting-group/news/huron-consulting-group-hurn-stock-looks-reasonable-following","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793882127.733,"origin":