king capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Free cash flow has compounded 7.3% a year over five years.","Forward indicators: a book-to-bill of 1.06 (orders outpacing sales), a backlog worth 17% of annual revenue and deferred revenue up 18%.","Capex runs only 0.3x depreciation (0.6% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is 22, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 2.7%, and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insiders have only sold over the past year (23 sales, net $4.8M sold).","It returns 6.3% a year to shareholders (6.3% in buybacks).","The share count has shrunk 6.4% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake."],"people":["With about 9,540 employees, each generates about $178K of revenue, 0.5x the Industrials median, and productivity has risen 7.1% a year.","That works out to $19K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $2.6M (15x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (3/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $5K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":65,"head":"Watch: Piotroski F-score 3/9.","pros":["FCF margin 10.8%","Revenue grew 14.3%/yr over 5y","Altman Z in the safe zone","P/FCF 14.4x vs sector 22.3x","4 analysts' mean target $202 (+21%)"],"cons":["Piotroski F-score 3/9"],"flags":[],"need":["the model rates it HOLD","only 14% below fair value"],"buy_below":164.8,"vc":{"base":193.89,"base_src":"dcf","bear":142.32,"bull":269.83,"alt_median":35.0,"n_alt":2,"gap":4.54,"dispersion":0.765,"level":"LOW","why":["models disagree (76% dispersion)","DCF is 454% above the other models' median ($35.00)"]},"med":{"pe":23.2692,"ev_ebitda":13.319,"pfcf":22.2778,"pb":3.0551,"roic":0.1001,"gross_margin":0.2851,"fcf_margin":0.068,"div_yield":0.0147}},"ticker":"HURN","date":"2026-11-06"}